  "gaps": [
    "The test-cards page does NOT map cardholder names (APRO, FUND, ...) to status_detail values; any such mapping would be inferred, so none is asserted.",
    "The test-cards page asks to fill 'Tipo y número de documento' but provides no document values for Mexico.",
    "No email or amount rule on the test-cards page; 'TEST' is described only as 'Usado para aplicar regla de montos' with no further detail.",
    "Outcome labels per cardholder name (approved/declined/other...) are our classification of the official Spanish status text.",
    "status_detail values come from the Checkout API (Payments) response-handling pages; the newer Orders API uses different codes (e.g. card_insufficient_amount, bad_filled_card_data) which were not read and are not included.",
    "cc_rejected_card_error appears only on the collection-results page, not the query-results page.",
    "Codes are listed with status 'rejected'; 'retryable' false only where docs say to use a different card/payment method.",
    "Category mapping is our own classification."
  ]
}
